-- A ledger write given to something larger. unstable's render says a write as
-- "V, recorded as C": its value comes first and no word of its own opens it,
-- so ", recorded as C" can attach to whatever comes before the value. Each
-- pair below records a different value and read alike before a write was
-- bracketed wherever it is part of something larger: an argument of a call, a
-- sentence's slot in any position, an operand of a comparison or of OR, a
-- branch of an IF, an element of a list.
-- The l4-cli-test block "l4 render brackets a ledger write given to something
-- larger" reads each row. No #EVAL here: render's output is the rules alone.

IMPORT prelude

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`plain1` x MEANS x PLUS 1

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`plain2` x y MEANS x PLUS y

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg pay %x%
`pay` x MEANS x PLUS 2

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
@nlg %x%
`bare` x MEANS x PLUS 4

GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
      y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`minimum of` x y MEANS x PLUS y

GIVEN a IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`fb` a MEANS a

-- A call with no sentence: its argument, last or not.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`call of a record` MEANS `plain1` (RECORD `balance` IS 100)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a call` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (`plain1` 100)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`second argument record` MEANS `plain2` 100 (RECORD `balance` IS 3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of two arguments` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (`plain2` 100 3)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`first argument record` MEANS `plain2` (RECORD `balance` IS 100) 3
GIVETH A NUMBER
`preposition of a record` MEANS `minimum of` 3 (RECORD `balance` IS 100)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a preposition` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (`minimum of` 3 100)
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition of a record` p IF `fb` (RECORD `flag` IS p)
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `record of a condition` p IF RECORD `flag` IS (`fb` p)

-- A sentence's slot that nothing follows.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sentence of a record` MEANS `pay` (RECORD `balance` IS 100)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a sentence` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (`pay` 100)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`bare of a record` MEANS `bare` (RECORD `balance` IS 100)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a bare` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (`bare` 100)

-- A comparison.
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `compare to a record` p IF p EQUALS (RECORD `flag` IS TRUE)
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `record of a comparison` p IF RECORD `flag` IS (p EQUALS TRUE)

-- Anywhere else inside something larger: an operand of OR in a slot, a
-- branch of an IF, an element of a list.
GIVEN xs IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`total` xs MEANS sum xs

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
@nlg %p% is shown
`shown` p MEANS p

GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `or of a record` p q IF `shown` (p OR (RECORD `flag` IS q))
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
      q IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `record of an or` p q IF `shown` (RECORD `flag` IS (p OR q))
GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`branch of a record` c MEANS `total` (LIST (IF c THEN 1 ELSE (RECORD `balance` IS 3)))
GIVEN c IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a branch` c MEANS `total` (LIST (RECORD `balance` IS (IF c THEN 1 ELSE 3)))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`element of a record` MEANS `total` (LIST 1, (RECORD `balance` IS 2))
GIVETH A NUMBER
`record of a list` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS (`total` (LIST 1, 2))

-- A write on its own reads as it did. One laid out as an item of a list is
-- part of something larger too, and keeps its brackets (a stated cost).
GIVETH A NUMBER
`a write alone` MEANS RECORD `balance` IS 100
GIVEN p IS A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an item of a list` p IF p AND (RECORD `flag` IS TRUE)
